# docs/book/02-types.md:66 § "Numbers" -- the float64 line on its own.
# language-reference.md:201 says "The type of an unadorned float literal is
# `float` (alias for `float64`)", and :416 lists `float` as an alias of float64.
# Expected: 3.141593
void main():
    float64 precise = 3.141592653589793
    print(f"{precise}")
